{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MdfF523NvJdRhjvDajxmDk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils/moreutils, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The project is an experiment in specification-driven code generation using an AI pipeline.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). cmd/ packages hold per-utility implementations, pkg/ holds shared libraries (sys, format, testutils, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil), magefiles/ drive the build. Differential testing via pkg/testutils compares Go binaries against g-prefixed GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Current state:** 33 releases (00.0–15.0) covering 111 utilities specified. Many utilities already implemented in earlier runs. The requirement_states field shows which SRD requirements are \"ready\" for generation.\n\n**Current focus:** Release 06.1 (environment and identity) is the earliest release with ready requirements. srd043-groups has R3.1–R3.3 remaining (R1.1–R2.3 were completed in tasks 5357/5358). srd039-env has all 12 requirements ready. srd040-printenv and srd041-id also have all requirements ready.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\n1. **srd043-groups R3.1–R3.3** — Complete the partially-implemented groups utility (3 remaining requirements)\n2. **srd039-env R1.1–R4.3** — Start and complete env (12 requirements, fits in 3 tasks of 4 each)\n3. printenv and id deferred to the next batch (4-task limit)\n\n## Weight Budget Checks\n\n```\nTask 0: srd039-env R1.1 (w=1), R1.2 (w=1), R1.3 (w=1), R2.1 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 1: srd039-env R2.2 (w=1), R2.3 (w=1), R3.1 (w=1), R3.2 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 2: srd039-env R3.3 (w=1), R4.1 (w=1), R4.2 (w=1), R4.3 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 3: srd043-groups R3.1 (w=1), R3.2 (w=1), R3.3 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1 = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\n(Weights assumed default=1; requirements.yaml not available in project_context.)\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] srd039-env R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1 (implementation)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd039-env.yaml (SRD for env -- focus on R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (differential testing pattern -- DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (SIGPIPE handler -- call InstallSIGPIPEHandler at start of main)\n      - CLAUDE.md (project conventions for building and testing)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/env/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: env utility implementation covering R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1\n      - path: cmd/env/env_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests for R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd039-env R1.1 per the SRD acceptance criteria\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd039-env R1.2 per the SRD acceptance criteria\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd039-env R1.3 per the SRD acceptance criteria\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd039-env R2.1 per the SRD acceptance criteria\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use the differential testing pattern from pkg/testutils with reference binary genv via exec.LookPath\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Call t.Skip if reference binary genv is not found in PATH\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Set LC_ALL=C in all differential test environments\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/env/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/env/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/env/ -count=1 passes (with t.Skip if reference binary genv not found)\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"All srd039-env R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1 acceptance criteria from the SRD are satisfied\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] srd039-env R2.2, R2.3, R3.1, R3.2 (implementation continued)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd039-env.yaml (SRD for env -- focus on R2.2, R2.3, R3.1, R3.2)\n      - cmd/env/main.go (existing implementation covering R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1)\n      - cmd/env/env_test.go (existing differential tests)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (differential testing pattern)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/env/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add R2.2, R2.3, R3.1, R3.2 functionality to existing implementation\n      - path: cmd/env/env_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential tests for R2.2, R2.3, R3.1, R3.2\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd039-env R2.2 per the SRD acceptance criteria\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd039-env R2.3 per the SRD acceptance criteria\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd039-env R3.1 per the SRD acceptance criteria\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd039-env R3.2 per the SRD acceptance criteria\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Extend the existing implementation in cmd/env/main.go -- do not rewrite code for R1.1-R2.1\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use the differential testing pattern from pkg/testutils with reference binary genv\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Preserve all existing tests in env_test.go when adding new test cases\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/env/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/env/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/env/ -count=1 passes (with t.Skip if reference binary genv not found